  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $f(1.25)=0.75$ and $f(1.75)=-0.50,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{′}(1.5).$\n\n${f}^{′}(1.5)≈$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=1.5$ with the step size $h=0.25.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(1.5) & ≈\\frac{f(1.5+0.25)-f(1.5-0.25)}{2(0.25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(1.75)-f(1.25)}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{-0.50-0.75}{0.5} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1.25)}{0.5} \\\\  & =-2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
